# Script function and purpose: dinit service description. Declarative, and
# like the SysV script it launches Sakura directly rather than through a
# getty, so it resolves no terminal-handover program.
type            = process
restart         = true
smooth-recovery = true
# Action purpose: bind Sakura to the terminal the installer reserved, and make
# that terminal its controlling terminal. dinit has no per-service device
# setting -- dinit-service(5) defines a console service's device as "the device
# to which dinit's standard output stream is connected", and inittab-line only
# "specifies the tty line that will be written to the \"utmp\" database" -- so
# shares-console on its own hands Sakura dinit's console rather than
# /dev/tty$DEFAULT_TTY. getActiveTty() asks TIOCGDEV which device is behind
# stdin, so that is the terminal Sakura would believe it owns: it would draw
# its prompt on the wrong one, or find none at all.
#
# setsid comes before the redirection on purpose. credentials(7): "The
# controlling terminal is established when the session leader first opens a
# terminal (unless the O_NOCTTY flag is specified when calling open(2))." The
# inner shell is therefore the session leader at the moment it opens the
# terminal, and the kernel assigns it on the open -- confirmed under strace:
# ctty acquired, zero TIOCSCTTY calls. Not `setsid --ctty`: when its ioctl is
# refused, it warns, exits 0 and never runs the program at all.
#
# The double quotes are dinit's own grouping, which it strips; the single
# quotes are not special to dinit and reach the shell intact. Every placeholder
# is replaced at install time, so the installed file contains no dollar sign at
# all and dinit's variable substitution has nothing to consume. The pid is
# preserved through both execs, so dinit supervises Sakura itself rather than a
# wrapper that has exited.
command         = /bin/sh -c "exec setsid /bin/sh -c 'exec $PREFIX_DIRECTORY/bin/$EXECUTABLE_NAME </dev/tty$DEFAULT_TTY >/dev/tty$DEFAULT_TTY 2>&1'"
depends-on      = login.target
termsignal      = HUP
# shares-console no longer decides which terminal Sakura gets -- the
# redirection above does -- but it is kept so Sakura neither queues behind nor
# blocks services that hold the console exclusively.
options         = shares-console
